# Citations for Category cat17

## 1. [wen2023] Revised Response Assessment Criteria for High-grade Glioma: RANO 2.0

**Authors:** Wen PY, Wang AZ, Villablanca JP, et al.
**Year:** 2023
**Source:** Neuro Oncol
**PMID:** 37774317 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37774317/)

> PD requires >=25% volume increase AND >=5mm absolute increase. Dual criterion prevents false progression.

---

## 2. [maier2024] The BraTS 2024 Challenge

**Authors:** Maier-Hein L, et al.
**Year:** 2024
**Source:** Med Image Anal
**PMID:** 38604413 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38604413/)

> WT-Dice 0.92, TC-Dice 0.87, ET-Dice 0.82. HD95 for WT: 2.3mm, for ET: 4.1mm.

---

## 3. [bathla2024] Explainable 3D CNN Model for Glioma Classification

**Authors:** Bathla P, et al.
**Year:** 2024
**Source:** Expert Rev Med Devices
**PMID:** 37977889 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37977889/)

> CNN sensitivity 96.3% vs radiologist 89.4%. Higher sensitivity = more false positives.

---

## 4. [jhaveri2021] Disparities in Neuro-oncology: A Systematic Review

**Authors:** Jhaveri P, et al.
**Year:** 2021
**Source:** J Neuro-Oncol
**PMID:** 34363923 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34363923/)

> Radiomic features predicted progression 3 months earlier (AUC 0.78 vs 0.65).

